+// The working space of the HDR TARGET, which is a third question again: the scene-referred path
+// can be running while r_SceneReferredDebug 1 deliberately leaves the buffer in Rec.709 for an
+// A/B. Everything that reads the target's CONTENTS - the per-view luminance weights, and any
+// future consumer that has to know which primaries it is looking at - keys on this, so the A/B
+// stays coherent instead of measuring 709 data with AP1 weights.
+bool CRendererResources::IsSceneReferredWorkingSpace()
+{
+	return IsSceneReferred() && CRenderer::CV_r_SceneReferredDebug != 1;
+}
